From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: turbinebmw <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Add lens-shading correction to 2x2
 binning

The Surface Pro 12 cameras lose most of their light towards the edges of
the frame: on a flat field the front camera's green channel falls to 0.4
of the centre at the side edges and 0.17 in the corners. With binning
showing the full field of view, the dark corners are plainly visible.

Read an optional `lensShading` section from the simple IPA tuning file: a
grid of gains per Bayer channel (R, Gr, Gb, B; 2048 = 1.0) spanning the
full pixel array, one table per illuminant with its white point as R/G,
B/G, and a strength that is applied as an exponent on the gains. Each
frame the debayer picks the table nearest the white balance, resamples it
when that changes, and scales raw values above black level: on the
binned path per output pixel and colour before temporal filtering, and on
the unbinned path per raw pixel as lines are copied for debayering (so the
statistics see shaded data too). An optional arraySize gives the pixel
array the grid spans when the input is a centred, scaled crop of it, as in
the OV13858's binned 2112x1188 mode.

The tables for the IMX681 and OV13858 come from the modules' Windows
tuning files. On a flat field at strength 1 the front camera stays within
0.8 of the centre in the corners; strength 0.7 keeps a gentle vignette
and less amplified corner noise, and won a blind comparison.
LIBCAMERA_SOFTISP_LSC overrides the strength, with 0 turning it off.

Unbinned shading needs unpacked raw with a 2-line Bayer pattern.
